course: dictionary
lesson: 13862
title: Who is in charge here?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A jurisdiction is the power to decide things, and the area where that power works. When you read «This crime happened in France, so it is outside our jurisdiction», the words outside and our tell you that the people speaking are not the ones who can decide. The clue is in the words around it.
explain: Ask two questions: who has the power, and where does it work? «The court has jurisdiction over this case» tells you the court is the one that decides. «Our town's police work only inside the town's jurisdiction» tells you the area is the town.
explain: Try your meaning in the sentence. If «the power to decide» fits, you have it. Jurisdiction is an uncountable noun, so we say «has jurisdiction» or «under the jurisdiction of», not «a jurisdiction of».
fact: Jurisdiction means the official power to make decisions and judgments about something.
fact: Jurisdiction can also mean the area or group where that power works, such as a state, a country or a court.
fact: «Under the jurisdiction of» means being controlled or decided by a particular police force, court or country.
fact: «Outside our jurisdiction» means not in our power to decide.
fact: A local school issue is not under the jurisdiction of the United Nations, because it is a local matter.
exercise: «This crime happened in France, so it is outside our jurisdiction.» What does outside our jurisdiction mean? | *Not under our power to decide | Inside a locked room | Right next to our school | Very far away on a map
exercise: «The court has jurisdiction over this case.» What does jurisdiction mean here? | A kind of fancy dress | A very long journey | The building where the court sits | *The power to decide the case
exercise: «Our town's police work only inside the town's jurisdiction.» What is the jurisdiction in this sentence? | The town's oldest school | A map of the country | The police officers' uniforms | *The area the police are in charge of
test: Why is a school squabble not under the jurisdiction of the UN? | *It is a local matter, outside the UN's power to decide | The UN is always in charge of everything | The school has a bigger jurisdiction than the UN | Squabbles are never reported
test: Which phrase means the same as outside our jurisdiction? | Inside our area of power | Beside our house | Under our desk | *Not in our area of power
exam: Pick the sentence that uses jurisdiction correctly. | *The police in this town have jurisdiction over crimes here | I had jurisdiction for lunch | Jurisdiction is a colour of paint | The dog's jurisdiction is a cosy bed
